@LJPost 5. The Italians enjoy this liberty of committing murder, etc. from the dispensations; (but it is otherwise with the English) because there is no dispensation...

Disperse.; Discutere.

@AC 719[end]. The evils which are to be dispersed, that is loosened and tempered by goods. @731.

@868. (They believe) that the evils and falsities with man are entirely dispersed and abolished; (whereas) there is not a single evil or falsity so dispersed as to be abolished...

@1059[2]. Such a cloud can be easily dispersed...

@1408[end]. With them, the fallacies taken from the sense of the letter are easily dispersed.

@1542. These (scientifics and pleasures) are first to be dispersed; and when they have been dispersed... @1563[2].

@1692. Temptations... are the means by which evils and falsities are loosened and dispersed.

@1888[end]. These reasonings are dispersed by...

