@--[4]. (Thus) the fear, dread, and terror with the evil are not from Divine good, but from Divine truth; and they exist when they do not receive Divine good, and yet receive Divine truth; also, Divine truth without good cannot penetrate towards the interiors; but merely sticks in the extremes...

@--[6]. For Divine good cannot be received by man, or Angel; but only by the Divine Human of the Lord (Signified); but Divine truth can be received... and in this Divine good can dwell, with a difference according to the reception.

